.TH VM 1 "2026" "vm-manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vm \- create and manage QEMU virtual machines from prebuilt OS images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vm
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vm
runs virtual machines from prebuilt cloud images, with a command set modelled
on Docker. Each machine is a detached QEMU process with its own writable disk
over the stored image, its own SSH key pair, and an account created by
cloud-init. A host port is always forwarded to the guest's SSH port, so
.B vm ssh
works without publishing one.
.PP
An image is named
.IR repository [: tag ][@ digest ],
as in
.BR debian:trixie .
The tag defaults to
.BR latest .
A digest pins the build: a reference whose digest does not match the
catalogue's build for the architecture is refused.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B images
List the images the catalogues name, with the size each occupies once fetched
and the catalogue naming it.
.BR \-\-local ", " \-\-remote
and
.BI \-\-catalogue " NAME"
limit the list to those catalogues; see
.BR vm\-config (5).
.TP
.BI inspect " IMAGE"
Show an image's build for this host's architecture, or for
.BR \-\-arch " ARCH" :
its other architectures, the catalogue naming it and any lower catalogues it
hides, its catalogue entry file, its source and digest, how its guest is
reached, where it is stored if pulled, and the machines using it.
.TP
.BI pull " IMAGE"
Fetch an image into the local store and verify it against the catalogue digest.
A compressed image is expanded with
.BR xz (1),
.BR gzip (1)
or
.BR zstd (1);
the digest covers the file as published.
.TP
.BI import " SOURCE IMAGE"
Name a file, or an
.B http
or
.B https
URL, as the image
.I repository:tag
in the
.B store
catalogue. A source compressed with
.BR xz (1),
.BR gzip (1)
or
.BR zstd (1)
is expanded. A disk image in any format
.BR qemu\-img (1)
reads is converted to qcow2; an ISO 9660 CD-ROM image is kept as it is. An
imported URL stays fetchable, so a pull converts it again; a downloaded image
that reads other files is refused.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-forget\-url
Keep no URL, so the image cannot be fetched again.
.TP
.BI \-\-digest " DIGEST"
Refuse a source whose digest, as published, differs.
.TP
.BI \-\-login " LOGIN"
.B cloud-init
for an image that takes a seed, or
.B none
(default).
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " ARCH"
The image's architecture, instead of this host's.
.TP
.BR \-\-firmware ", " \-\-cpu ", " \-\-machine ", " \-\-disk
Hardware the image needs, as for
.BR run .
.TP
.BI \-\-description " TEXT"
The image's description, which otherwise names the source.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Replace an image of the same name in the
.B store
catalogue.
.RE
.TP
.BI export " IMAGE FILE"
Copy a held image to
.IR FILE ,
in the format it is stored in, checking it against its digest where that
covers the stored file. A
.I FILE
without an image suffix gains one, such as
.B .qcow2
or
.BR .iso ;
a directory gains a file named
.I repository-tag
with that suffix; a suffix for another format is refused.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-compress " [" \fISCHEME\fR ]
Compress the file with
.BR xz (1),
or with
.B gzip
or
.B zstd
if named, adding
.BR .xz ,
.B .gz
or
.BR .zst .
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " ARCH"
Export another architecture's build.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Replace an existing file.
.RE
.TP
.B config
Show the config file's path and every setting and catalogue, marking defaults.
With no file, say where one would be created; none is created until a change is
made.
.RS
.TP
.B config path
Print the config file's path.
.TP
.BI "config get " KEY
Print a setting's value.
.TP
.BI "config set " "KEY VALUE"
Set
.BR auto_pull ,
.B add_ssh_config
or
.BR default_user .
An invalid value is refused.
.TP
.BI "config unset " KEY
Remove a setting, restoring its default.
.TP
.BI "config add remote " "NAME URL" "\fR [\fB\-\-path \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-before \fINAME\fR]"
Add a remote catalogue, last or before the one named. Added first, it follows
.BR project ,
which stays in use until removed.
.TP
.BI "config add local " "NAME DIRECTORY" "\fR [\fB\-\-before \fINAME\fR]"
Add a local catalogue, last or before the one named.
.TP
.BI "config remove remote" "\fR|\fPlocal NAME"
Remove a catalogue.
.RE
.IP
A change rewrites the file in a standard layout; comments are not kept.
.TP
.BR update " [" \fINAME\fR ]
Refresh every remote catalogue, or the one named. A catalogue that cannot be
fetched keeps its previous copy, and the command exits 1.
.TP
.BI run " IMAGE"
Create and start a machine. See
.BR "OPTIONS FOR RUN" .
A machine run from a CD-ROM image gets a blank disk and boots the CD-ROM until
the disk holds a system, so an installer's reboot starts the installed system.
.TP
.BI start " NAME"
Start a stopped machine. Takes
.BR \-\-memory ", " \-\-cpus ", " \-\-publish ", " \-\-volume ", " \-\-user ,
.BR \-\-disk\-size ", " \-\-firmware ", " \-\-cpu ", " \-\-machine ", " \-\-disk ,
.B \-\-password
and
.B \-\-add\-ssh\-config
as
.B run
does; each change persists, and settings not given are kept. Forwards and shares
are replaced as a list.
.BR \-\-no\-publish ", " \-\-no\-volume ", " \-\-no\-password
and
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-config
remove them.
.B \-\-eject
removes the CD-ROM, after which the machine no longer needs its image. A running
machine cannot be changed.
.IP
A disk prepared for one firmware does not boot under the other, and a guest
without a driver for its disk controller does not find its disk; changing the
setting back restores the machine. FreeBSD reads a new account or password only
on first boot, so give those to
.BR run .
.TP
.BI ssh " NAME " [\fICOMMAND\fR]
Open a shell on a machine, or run a command in it, through
.BR ssh (1),
so
.I ~/.ssh/config
and the agent apply.
.TP
.BI cp " FROM TO"
Copy files to or from a machine, writing one side as
.IR NAME:PATH .
.TP
.B ps
List running machines;
.B \-\-all
includes stopped ones.
.B \-\-follow
refreshes every second. Memory and disk are shown as used out of allotted; the
document formats give
.IR memory ", " memory_used ", " disk " and " disk_used
in mebibytes.
.TP
.BI stop " NAME"
Ask the guest to shut down, and kill it after
.B \-\-timeout
seconds (default 30).
.TP
.BI pause " NAME"
Stop a machine's processors. Nothing is saved, so a paused machine does not
survive a host reboot or
.BR "vm kill" .
.B vm ssh
and
.B vm cp
refuse a paused machine.
.TP
.BI resume " NAME"
Resume a paused machine.
.TP
.BI kill " NAME"
Stop a machine without telling the guest.
.TP
.BI console " NAME"
Attach the terminal to the machine's serial console. Ctrl-] detaches. One
terminal can attach at a time.
.TP
.BI screen " NAME"
Open
.BR xtigervncviewer (1)
on the machine's screen. Without a display, or in a document format, print the
VNC socket and an
.BR ssh (1)
command that forwards it.
.TP
.BI screenshot " NAME " [\fIFILE\fR]
Save the machine's screen as a PNG, to
.I FILE
or
.IR NAME.png .
.TP
.B gui
Open the window,
.BR vmg (1),
which is installed by the vm\-manager\-gui package.
.TP
.BI logs " NAME"
Show the machine's console output from every boot.
.B \-\-follow
streams it until the machine stops;
.BI \-n ", " \-\-lines " COUNT"
shows only the last lines.
.TP
.BI rmi " IMAGE"
Delete an image name from the local store. A catalogue image is listed again as
unfetched; an image made by
.B vm clone
or
.B vm import
loses its catalogue entry. Entries in other local catalogues are left in place. An image in use by a machine is refused without
.BR \-\-force .
Names for identical images share one file, which is deleted with the last name.
.TP
.BI clone " NAME IMAGE"
Save a machine's disk as the image
.IR repository:tag ,
flattening it and then verifying it. A running guest is paused meanwhile unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.BI \-\-description " TEXT"
sets the image's description, which otherwise names the source machine.
.TP
.BI rm " NAME"
Delete a machine and its disk.
.B \-\-force
removes a running one.
.TP
.BI prune " " [\fBmachines\fR|\fBimages\fR]
Remove machines and images nothing needs: machines first, then images, or only
the one named.
.B \-\-dry\-run
lists what would be removed. Running and paused machines, images a machine
uses, and images that cannot be fetched again are never removed.
.RS
.TP
Removed by default
Machines whose image is not held and cannot be fetched; sockets left by
machines that are not running; image files no catalogue entry names; records of
pulled images whose file is gone; and partial files from pulls, clones or imports
untouched for an hour.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Also every stopped machine, including those whose record cannot be read, and
every pulled image no machine uses.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS FOR RUN
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
The machine's name. Invented if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-memory " AMOUNT"
Memory, in mebibytes unless suffixed with M or G. Default 2G.
.TP
.BI \-\-cpus " COUNT"
Processors. Default 2.
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-publish " HOST:GUEST"
Forward a host port to a guest port. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-v ", " \-\-volume " HOST:GUEST"
Share a host directory with the guest over virtiofs, mounted at every boot.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
The account to create in the guest. Defaults to
.B default_user
in
.BR vm\-config (5),
or
.BR vm .
.TP
.BI \-\-disk\-size " SIZE"
Grow the disk to this size, such as 40G. For a CD-ROM image, the size of the
blank disk; default 20G.
.TP
.BI \-\-pull " WHEN"
.BR always ", " missing " (default) or " never .
.TP
.BI \-\-firmware " FIRMWARE"
.BR bios " or " uefi ,
overriding the image.
.TP
.BI \-\-cpu " MODEL"
A QEMU CPU model, such as
.BR Penryn,+avx ,
overriding the image. Most images use
.BR max .
.TP
.BI \-\-machine " TYPE"
.BR q35 " or " pc ,
overriding the image.
.TP
.BI \-\-disk " CONTROLLER"
.BR virtio ", " ide " (pc only) or " sata " (q35 only),"
overriding the image.
.TP
.B \-\-password
Set a password for logging in at
.BR "vm console" ,
read from the terminal twice or as one line of standard input. SSH still
accepts only the machine's key. Refused for an image without cloud-init.
.TP
.B \-\-add\-ssh\-config
Let plain
.BR ssh (1),
.BR scp (1)
and
.BR rsync (1)
reach the machine by name. The entry is kept as
.I ssh_config
in the machine's directory, rewritten at each start and removed with the
machine. An
.B Include
line for all entries is added to the top of
.IR ~/.ssh/config ,
creating the file if needed. A name already used by a
.B Host
there is refused, as is an image without cloud-init.
.B add_ssh_config
in
.BR vm\-config (5)
makes this the default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-config
Add no entry, whatever
.BR vm\-config (5)
says.
.SH OUTPUT
Commands write text by default, or a document with
.B \-\-format json
or
.BR "\-\-format yaml" .
A document is the only thing on standard output; progress and errors go to
standard error. Errors carry a stable
.BR kind .
.B vm logs \-\-follow
and
.B vm console
accept only text.
.B vm ssh
hands the terminal to
.BR ssh (1);
scripts can read
.B ssh_port
and
.B user
from
.BR "vm ps \-\-format json" .
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
The package installs completion for bash, zsh and fish. Without it, load it with
one of:
.RS
.nf
source <(COMPLETE=bash vm)
source <(COMPLETE=zsh vm)
COMPLETE=fish vm | source
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vm/config.toml
Optional settings. See
.BR vm\-config (5).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/vm/images
The image store.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/vm/catalogues/NAME
Each remote catalogue, as last fetched.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/vm/local
The
.B store
catalogue, holding entries for images made by
.B vm clone
and
.BR "vm import" .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/vm/instances
One private directory per machine: its disk, key, console log, record, SSH
config entry and UEFI variable store.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
Gains an
.B Include
line when a machine is first given
.BR \-\-add\-ssh\-config .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vm
Monitor, console, screen and share sockets.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VM_FORMAT
The default output format.
.TP
.B COMPLETE
A shell name; prints completion for that shell.
.TP
.B VM_CATALOGUE
A catalogue directory used in place of every remote catalogue.
.SH NOTES
A guest can
.BR ping (8)
only if
.I /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ping_group_range
on the host includes one of the user's groups. Only echo requests pass, so
.BR traceroute (1)
sees nothing past the host.
.PP
An installer booted under UEFI records its boot entry in the machine's own
variable store. An image cloned from that disk boots elsewhere only if the
installer also placed the removable-media loader, such as
.IR \eEFI\eBOOT\eBOOTX64.EFI .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vmg (1),
.BR vm\-config (5),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR scp (1),
.BR qemu\-system\-x86_64 (1),
.BR qemu\-img (1),
.BR virtiofsd (1),
.BR xtigervncviewer (1)
